/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  Membrane: CA30, a cellulose acetate nanofiltration membrane -- CASE-
  LOCAL, as Bowen & Mohammad characterised it.

  The pore parameters Bowen & Mohammad determined for CA30 (W.R. Bowen,
  A.W. Mohammad, "Diafiltration by nanofiltration: prediction and
  optimization", AIChE J. 44 (1998) 1799), as Geraldes & Alves quote them
  (J. Membr. Sci. 321 (2008) 172-182, section 4.1):
    pore radius                      0.63 nm
    equivalent thickness dx/A_k      6.2 um  -> porosityOverThickness 1/6.2e-6
  "Equivalent thickness" is the paper's own word for the active-layer
  thickness over the surface porosity (its section 2: dx_e = dx/A_k), the
  length the pore model sees; Choupo's record states the same thing as
  A_k/dx.  No pore dielectric constant: the paper ran this case with
  eps_p = eps_b, so there is no dielectric exclusion (Born OFF).

  THE FIXED CHARGE IS NOT HERE.  Bowen & Mohammad found it to depend on
  the feed and fitted it to their data (the paper's Eq. 43):
      c_X = -9.03 - 3.29 (3 c_Dye + c_Cl)        [mol/m3]
  so it has no one value a record could carry; every op of the case
  declares the c_X of its own feed (`chargeDensity`), its arithmetic
  written beside it.

  A_w is not read by the props bench (it imposes J_v, which the paper's
  Eqs. 44-45 give for each feed); a value is carried because the record
  grammar requires one.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name           CA30_BowenMohammad;
kind           NF;
manufacturer   "CA30 (cellulose acetate), as characterised by Bowen & Mohammad (1998)";

A_w            1.0e-5  m/s/bar;     // not read at an imposed J_v

poreModel
{
    poreRadius             6.3e-10;            // m
    porosityOverThickness  161290.32258064516; // 1/m  (= 1/6.2e-6 m)
}
